      {"t":"fill","q":"Coffee __ tea?","p":"Caffè o tè?","a":["or"],"o":["so","but","because"],"why":"Per scegliere tra due cose, \"or\"."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Sono stanco ma felice","a":["I'm tired but happy","I am tired but happy","I'm tired but I'm happy","I am tired but I'm happy","I am tired but I am happy","I'm tired but I am happy"],"hint":"tired · but · happy — usa but","x":["so"],"why":"«Ma» è \"but\"."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Sono rimasto a casa perché pioveva","a":["I stayed home because it was raining","I stayed at home because it was raining","I stayed home because it rained","I stayed at home because it rained"],"hint":"stayed home · because · rain — con soggetto","x":["so"],"why":"Dopo \"because\" serve un soggetto: \"it was raining\", mai \"because was raining\"."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Lui non è venuto per la pioggia (usa il past simple)","a":["He didn't come because of the rain","He did not come because of the rain"],"hint":"didn't · come · because of — la pioggia","x":["came"],"why":"Negativa al passato con l'ausiliare \"didn't\"; \"because of\" va prima di un nome."}
